<!--
  ============================================================================
  JawaIon_FieldOurOwnGun.xml               Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-22
  ============================================================================

  🔴 THE DEFECT, measured 2026-08-22 against the 2026-08-21 def dump:

    JawaIon_Damage      requested by  0 pawn kinds
    Jawa_IonWeapon      requested by  3   (TradeMoot Heavy, Leader, Specialist)
    Jawa_IonWeaponLight requested by  1   (TradeMoot Grunt)
    KotORRanged_ion     requested by  4   (all four TradeMoot kinds)

  `JawaIon_Blaster` — the campaign's signature weapon, the one thing canon says
  Jawas MANUFACTURE, built in our own `JawaIonWeapons` mod with a bespoke
  `DamageWorker_IonBuildup` — carries the tag `JawaIon_Damage`, and NOTHING ASKS
  FOR IT. It is a craftable curio behind research that no pawn ever spawns with.

  ⚠️ AND THE GUNS THEY DO CARRY ARE NOT ION IN THE SENSE THE DESIGN MEANT.
  Read from the DamageDefs, not from the tag names:

    IW_IonBullet          (Jawa_IonWeapon)   harmsHealth TRUE · Sharp · Gunshot
                                             · makesBlood TRUE   -> shoots bullets
    guy762_RangedDamage_ion (KotORRanged_ion) harmsHealth TRUE · Heat · Burn
    OuterRim_Ion          (ORIonRifle)       harmsHealth false · causeStun true
    JawaIon_Damage        (OURS)             harmsHealth FALSE · makesBlood false
                                             · externalViolence FALSE
                                             · externalViolenceForMechanoids TRUE
                                             · combatLogRules Damage_EMP
                                             · JawaIonWeapons.DamageWorker_IonBuildup

  ⇒ Only OUR gun is the capture weapon `setting_physics.md` L16 describes.
  The Trade Moot currently fields somebody else's ion-BRANDED rifles that kill
  people normally.

  WHY THIS IS A PATCH AND NOT AN EDIT AT SOURCE
  ==============================================
  `Defs/PawnKindDefs/JawaFactionRoster.xml` is EMITTED by
  `src/RimMandrake/Utils/gen_pawnkind_roster.py` (rows 226-229 hold these four
  kinds). A hand edit there dies at the next run — the same reason
  `JawaXenotype_Repoint.xml` exists.
  🔑 ⇒ THIS PATCH IS A STOPGAP. The durable fix is to add "JawaIon_Damage" to the
  tag lists on generator rows 227-229 and re-emit. Filed as
  `IONBLASTER_INTO_THE_GENERATOR_1`.

  WHO GETS IT, AND THE ARITHMETIC — measured, not assumed
  ========================================================
    JawaIon_Blaster  MarketValue 420

    TradeMoot Grunt       weaponMoney 250-300   -> CANNOT AFFORD  ⛔ not patched
    TradeMoot Heavy       weaponMoney 450-540   -> affordable      ✅
    TradeMoot Specialist  weaponMoney 900-1080  -> affordable      ✅
    TradeMoot Leader      weaponMoney 900-1080  -> affordable      ✅

  ⛔ The Grunt is deliberately EXCLUDED. `PawnWeaponGenerator` filters candidates
  by market value against `weaponMoney`, so adding the tag at 250-300 against a
  420 weapon would be a silent no-op — a tag that looks like a fix and hands the
  pawn nothing. Raising the Grunt's budget instead would break the row the
  guidance doc is proudest of: the Jawa have the lowest weapon budget on the map.
  ⇒ The hand-built blaster reads as the mark of a senior Jawa, not standard issue.

  ⚠️ NOTE FOR WHOEVER TUNES THE GRUNT NEXT: its `Jawa_IonWeaponLight` tag resolves
  to `IW_Gun_IonPistol` (800) and `IW_Gun_IonPDW` (1000), BOTH above its 300
  ceiling. Its only affordable ion today is `guy762_ionpistol` (200) via
  `KotORRanged_ion`. That is a second, separate defect.

  SAFETY
  ======
  Conditional on each def existing, so a rename or a regeneration makes this a
  silent no-op rather than red text. `PatchOperationAdd` APPENDS to the existing
  `weaponTags` list; the current tags survive.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="Jawa_TradeMoot_Heavy"]/weaponTags</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="Jawa_TradeMoot_Heavy"]/weaponTags</xpath>
      <value><li>JawaIon_Damage</li></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="Jawa_TradeMoot_Specialist"]/weaponTags</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="Jawa_TradeMoot_Specialist"]/weaponTags</xpath>
      <value><li>JawaIon_Damage</li></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="Jawa_TradeMoot_Leader"]/weaponTags</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="Jawa_TradeMoot_Leader"]/weaponTags</xpath>
      <value><li>JawaIon_Damage</li></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
